 "A1_fill_without_prior_touch": {
  "classification": "EXPECTED_SEMANTIC_CASE",
  "n_total": 1010,
  "mechanism": "The producer tests far-edge fill independently of range overlap. FvgDetector::process_bar: touch is emitted only when `bar.h >= zone.lower && bar.l <= zone.upper` and the zone is not yet touched; fill is emitted when bullish `bar.l <= zone.lower` (bearish `bar.h >= zone.upper`); the fill payload records `first_touch_observed: zone.touched`; the zone is then removed from active state. A bar that trades entirely beyond the far edge (bullish: high < zone.lower; bearish: low > zone.upper) reaches the far edge without its range ever overlapping the zone, so the lake legitimately emits fill with no first-touch and first_touch_observed=false. The director reconciliation premise \"a filling bar necessarily overlaps the zone\" is false for beyond-edge bars; the frozen authority semantics themselves (fill = low reaches lower edge / high reaches upper edge; touch = range overlaps) admit this case. The research reconstruction (fvg_e1.rs) processed these rows faithfully: it recorded the fill, recorded no touch, and never fabricated a touch.",
