  "reading": "Median paired receipt latency is ~0.09-0.12 s for both touch and fill at every stratum; p95 is 0.34-1.63 s. The max (~1.8e8 ms, about 2.1 days) is session-gap receipt (a bar completing at a session close becomes known at the next receipt). No stratum, including 1h, shows a distinctively large paired delay: the frozen tables known-vs-market quantile divergences (e.g. 1h fill p75 known 104,400,134 ms vs market 118,800,000 ms) arise from comparing separately computed quantiles of formation->event known and formation->event market durations, whose difference mixes formation receipt latency with event receipt latency. The paired distributions above are the required descriptive basis; any clock-dependence claim still requires a defined anchor-clock contract in E1B."
